---
import BackLink from "../BackLink.astro";

const parts = [
  { id: "aperture", number: "01", label: "Aperture" },
  { id: "storage", number: "02", label: "Battery & SD cards" },
  { id: "cap", number: "03", label: "Lens cap" },
];
---

<camera-explorer>
  <main class="camera-page">
    <header class="page-header">
      <a href="/" class="wordmark"
        >Liam Sullivan <span>/ a little detour</span></a
      >
      <BackLink label="Exit" href="/" />
    </header>

    <section class="introduction" aria-labelledby="camera-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <span class="status-dot"></span> You found the easter egg
      </p>
      <h1 id="camera-title">A closer look.</h1>
      <p class="intro-copy">
        A few small parts. A whole different way of seeing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="explorer-layout">
      <section
        class="stage"
        aria-label="Interactive Sony α7 III camera diagram"
      >
        <div class="stage-caption">
          <span>SONY α7 III</span><span>INTERACTIVE STUDY / 001</span>
        </div>
        <div class="viewport" data-viewport>
          <div class="scene-status" data-status role="status">
            Preparing your camera…
          </div>
          <div class="hotspots" data-hotspots hidden>
            {
              parts.map((part) => (
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class={`hotspot hotspot-${part.id}`}
                  data-part={part.id}
                  data-hotspot={part.id}
                  aria-label={`Explore ${part.label}`}
                  aria-pressed="false"
                >
                  <>
                    <span class="hotspot-number">{part.number}</span>
                    <span class="hotspot-label">{part.label}</span>
                  </>
                </button>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage-footer">
          <p id="orbit-instructions">
            <svg
              width="15"
              height="15"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              aria-hidden="true"
              ><path
                d="M7 7a7 7 0 0 1 12 5M17 17A7 7 0 0 1 5 12M7 3v4H3m14 14v-4h4"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.5"></path></svg
            ><span data-orbit-hint>Drag to rotate · Scroll to zoom</span>
          </p>
          <button type="button" class="text-button" data-reset
            >Reset view <span aria-hidden="true">↺</span></button
          >
        </div>
      </section>

      <aside class="field-notes" aria-label="Camera field notes">
        <div class="notes-header">
          <span class="eyebrow">Field notes</span><span
            class="note-index"
            data-note-index>00 / 03</span
          >
        </div>
        <div data-panel="overview">
          <p class="small-label">Meet the camera</p>
          <h2>A tool for <br />paying attention.</h2>
          <p>
            A camera turns light into a photograph. The interesting part is how
            much control you have along the way.
          </p>
          <p>
            This is a hands-on look at the Sony α7 III. Turn it around, then
            pick a numbered part to see what’s happening inside.
          </p>
          <dl class="camera-specs">
            <div><dt>Camera</dt><dd>Sony α7 III</dd></div><div>
              <dt>System</dt><dd>Full-frame · Mirrorless</dd>
            </div><div><dt>Mount</dt><dd>Sony E-mount</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div class="note-tip">
            <span aria-hidden="true">↖</span><p>
              Follow your curiosity.<br /><span
                >Choose a part below or on the camera.</span
              >
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-panel="aperture" hidden>
          <p class="small-label">01 / Inside the lens</p>
          <h2>Let there <br />be light.</h2>
          <p>
            The aperture is an adjustable opening inside the lens. Its
            overlapping blades control how much light passes through.
          </p>
          <p>
            A lower f-number means a wider opening and a shallower depth of
            field. A higher f-number gives a smaller opening and more depth of
            field, all else equal.
          </p>
          <div class="aperture-control">
            <label for="aperture-range"
              >Try the aperture <output
                for="aperture-range"
                data-aperture-output>f/2.8</output
              ></label
            >
            <input
              id="aperture-range"
              type="range"
              min="0"
              max="5"
              step="1"
              value="0"
              aria-valuetext="f/2.8"
            />
            <div class="range-labels">
              <span>Wider / more light</span><span>Smaller / less light</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="technical-note">
            The front glass fades away in this view to reveal a simplified iris.
            The lens and aperture range are illustrative.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div data-panel="storage" hidden>
          <p class="small-label">02 / Power & memory</p>
          <h2>Keep the <br />moment.</h2>
          <p>
            The side door protects two memory-card slots. You can configure the
            camera to record to both cards for a backup, or switch cards when
            one fills up.
          </p>
          <dl class="camera-specs">
            <div><dt>Slot 1 · lower</dt><dd>SD · UHS-I / UHS-II</dd></div><div>
              <dt>Slot 2 · upper</dt><dd>SD · UHS-I</dd>
            </div><div><dt>Battery · underneath</dt><dd>NP-FZ100</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p>
            The battery has its own door on the bottom of the grip. The opened
            diagram shows the two separate compartments.
          </p>
          <p class="technical-note">
            Turn the camera off and wait for the access lamp to go out before
            removing a memory card.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div data-panel="cap" hidden>
          <p class="small-label">03 / Between photographs</p>
          <h2>A little <br />protection.</h2>
          <p>
            Simple, but useful: the lens cap protects the front glass from dust,
            fingerprints, and scratches while the camera is packed away.
          </p>
          <p>
            Pinch the two center tabs to release it from the lens rim. A
            center-pinch design is easy to reach even with a lens hood attached.
          </p>
          <div class="note-tip">
            <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><p>
              Match the lens, not the body.<br /><span
                >Cap size follows the lens’s filter diameter, marked with a ⌀
                symbol.</span
              >
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="technical-note">
            The cap is shown detached so you can explore the glass and iris
            behind it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="back-to-camera" data-back hidden
          ><kbd>Esc</kbd> Back to the whole camera <span aria-hidden="true"
            >↗</span
          ></button
        >
      </aside>
    </div>

    <nav class="part-navigation" aria-label="Explore camera parts">
      {
        parts.map((part) => (
          <button type="button" data-part={part.id} aria-pressed="false">
            <>
              <span class="part-number">{part.number}</span>
              <span>{part.label}</span>
              <span class="part-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                ↗
              </span>
            </>
          </button>
        ))
      }
    </nav>

    <footer class="page-footer">
      <p>Made for the joy of looking closer.</p><p>
        Simplified 3D study <span>·</span>
        <a
          class="guide-link"
          href="https://helpguide.sony.net/ilc/1720/v1/en/index.html"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer">Sony α7 III guide ↗</a
        >
      </p>
    </footer>
    <p class="sr-only" data-announcement aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
    </p>
    <noscript
      ><p class="noscript-note">
        Enable JavaScript to rotate the 3D camera and explore its parts.
      </p></noscript
    >
  </main>
</camera-explorer>

<script>
  import { initializeExplorer } from "./explorer";

  class CameraExplorerElement extends HTMLElement {
    private cleanup?: () => void;
    connectedCallback() {
      this.cleanup = initializeExplorer(this);
    }
    disconnectedCallback() {
      this.cleanup?.();
    }
  }
  if (!customElements.get("camera-explorer")) {
    customElements.define("camera-explorer", CameraExplorerElement);
  }
</script>

<style>
  camera-explorer {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text-color);
    --camera-accent: #e9a06c;
  }
  .camera-page {
    width: min(1500px, 100%);
    min-height: 100svh;
    margin: auto;
    padding: 0 3.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .page-header {
    height: 92px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .wordmark {
    color: #eee;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .wordmark span {
    color: #777;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-left: 12px;
  }
  .introduction {
    padding: 2.25rem 0 2.5rem;
  }
  .eyebrow,
  .stage-caption,
  .note-index,
  .small-label,
  .part-number,
  .hotspot-number,
  .range-labels,
  .technical-note,
  .page-footer {
    font-family: "Martian Mono Variable", monospace;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    color: var(--camera-accent);
    font-size: 9px;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .status-dot {
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4.5vw, 4.5rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    text-align: left;
    margin: 15px 0 14px;
  }
  .intro-copy {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #969696;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .explorer-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 310px;
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 450px;
    border-top: 1px solid #303030;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #303030;
  }
  .stage {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
    position: relative;
  }
  .stage-caption {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 22px 28px 0 0;
    color: #737373;
    font-size: 8px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .stage-caption span:first-child {
    color: #b6b6b6;
  }
  .viewport {
    position: relative;
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 380px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .viewport :global(canvas) {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: block;
    touch-action: none;
    cursor: grab;
  }
  .viewport :global(canvas:active) {
    cursor: grabbing;
  }
  .viewport :global(canvas:focus-visible) {
    outline-offset: -3px;
  }
  .scene-status {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    color: #aaa;
    font-size: 13px;
    text-align: center;
    width: min(320px, 90%);
    z-index: 2;
  }
  .hotspots {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .hotspot {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    pointer-events: auto;
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: #ddd;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    padding: 8px;
    border-radius: 30px;
    cursor: pointer;
    will-change: transform;
  }
  .hotspot-number {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 27px;
    height: 27px;
    border: 1px solid #bd835c;
    background: #171411e8;
    border-radius: 50%;
    font-size: 9px;
    color: #f4b88d;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px #e9a06c08;
  }
  .hotspot-label {
    padding: 4px 6px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-size: 10px;
    background: #0f0f0fd9;
  }
  .hotspot:hover .hotspot-number,
  .hotspot[aria-pressed="true"] .hotspot-number {
    background: var(--camera-accent);
    color: #151515;
  }
  .stage-footer {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 0 28px 22px 0;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .stage-footer p {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: #888;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .text-button {
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    color: #aaa;
    font-size: 11px;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 8px 0 8px 8px;
  }
  .text-button span {
    margin-left: 8px;
  }
  .text-button:hover {
    color: white;
  }
  .field-notes {
    border-left: 1px solid #303030;
    padding: 24px 0 24px 30px;
  }
  .notes-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 34px;
  }
  .notes-header .eyebrow {
    color: #8d8d8d;
    font-size: 8px;
  }
  .note-index {
    color: #737373;
    font-size: 8px;
  }
  .small-label {
    color: var(--camera-accent);
    font-size: 8px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.045em;
    margin: 0 0 13px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 31px;
    text-align: left;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .field-notes p:not(.eyebrow, .small-label, .technical-note) {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #a0a0a0;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .camera-specs {
    margin: 23px 0;
    font-size: 10px;
  }
  .camera-specs div {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 10px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #272727;
  }
  .camera-specs dt {
    color: #838383;
  }
  .camera-specs dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: #ccc;
    text-align: right;
  }
  .note-tip {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  .note-tip > span {
    color: var(--camera-accent);
    font-size: 20px;
  }
  .field-notes .note-tip p {
    color: #ccc;
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  .note-tip p span {
    color: #858585;
  }
  .technical-note {
    color: #858585;
    font-size: 8px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 20px 0 0;
  }
  .aperture-control {
    margin: 24px 0;
  }
  .aperture-control label {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    color: #ccc;
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  output {
    color: var(--camera-accent);
    font-family: monospace;
  }
  input[type="range"] {
    display: block;
    accent-color: var(--camera-accent);
    width: 100%;
    margin: 20px 0 13px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .range-labels {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    color: #858585;
    font-size: 7px;
  }
  .back-to-camera {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    width: 100%;
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #303030;
    background: transparent;
    color: #ccc;
    margin-top: 24px;
    padding: 18px 0 0;
    font-size: 10px;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .back-to-camera > span {
    margin-left: auto;
    color: var(--camera-accent);
  }
  kbd {
    font:
      9px "Martian Mono Variable",
      monospace;
    border: 1px solid #444;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 5px;
    color: #aaa;
  }
  .part-navigation {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    border-bottom: 1px solid #303030;
  }
  .part-navigation button {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 18px;
    padding: 25px 26px;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    color: #bababa;
    font-size: 13px;
    text-align: left;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      background 180ms,
      color 180ms;
  }
  .part-navigation button + button {
    border-left: 1px solid #303030;
  }
  .part-number {
    color: #777;
    font-size: 9px;
  }
  .part-arrow {
    margin-left: auto;
    color: #777;
  }
  .part-navigation button:hover,
  .part-navigation button[aria-pressed="true"] {
    background: #191612;
    color: #f3bc93;
  }
  .part-navigation button[aria-pressed="true"] .part-number,
  .part-navigation button[aria-pressed="true"] .part-arrow {
    color: var(--camera-accent);
  }
  .page-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 15px;
    padding: 25px 0;
  }
  .page-footer p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #797979;
    font-size: 8px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .page-footer span {
    margin: 0 10px;
  }
  .guide-link {
    color: #999;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .guide-link:hover {
    color: #ccc;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .noscript-note {
    padding: 1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  [hidden] {
    display: none !important;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1500px) {
    .viewport {
      min-height: 480px;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .camera-page {
      padding: 0 2rem;
    }
    .explorer-layout {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 270px;
    }
    .field-notes {
      padding-left: 24px;
    }
    .hotspot-label {
      display: none;
    }
    .stage-caption {
      font-size: 7px;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .camera-page {
      padding: 0 1.25rem;
    }
    .page-header {
      height: 72px;
    }
    .wordmark {
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    .wordmark span {
      font-size: 10px;
      margin-left: 5px;
    }
    .introduction {
      padding: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
    }
    .intro-copy {
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    .explorer-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .stage-caption {
      padding-right: 0;
    }
    .viewport {
      flex: none;
      height: 350px;
      min-height: 0;
    }
    .stage-footer {
      padding-right: 0;
      padding-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .stage-footer p,
    .text-button {
      font-size: 10px;
    }
    .field-notes {
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid #303030;
      padding: 22px 0;
    }
    .notes-header {
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }
    h2 {
      font-size: 28px;
    }
    h2 br {
      display: none;
    }
    .field-notes p:not(.eyebrow, .small-label, .technical-note) {
      max-width: 540px;
    }
    .part-navigation {
      order: 0;
    }
    .part-navigation button {
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 20px 10px;
      font-size: 10px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .part-number {
      font-size: 8px;
    }
    .part-arrow {
      display: none;
    }
    .page-footer {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 22px 0;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .part-navigation button {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
